oplet (LD)</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">sorting nexin 14</Keyword></KeywordList><CoiStatement>The authors declare no competing interest.</CoiStatement></MedlineCitation><PubmedData><History><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pubmed"><Year>2020</Year><Month>12</Month><Day>15</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>0</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="medline"><Year>2020</Year><Month>12</Month><Day>15</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>1</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="entrez"><Year>2020</Year><Month>12</Month><Day>14</Day><Hour>10</Hour><Minute>44</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pmc-release"><Year>2021</Year><Month>6</Month><Day>11</Day></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>ppublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">33310904</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC7777019</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1073/pnas.2011124117</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pii">2011124117</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Schaffer J. E., Lipotoxicity: When tissues overeat. Curr. Opin. Lipidol. 14, 281&#x2013;287 (2003).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">12840659</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Lelliott C., Vidal-Puig A. J., Lipotoxicity, an imbalance between lipogenesis de novo and fatty acid oxidation. Int. J. Obes. Relat. Metab. Disord. 28 (suppl. 4), S22&#x2013;S28 (2004).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">15592482</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Ertunc M. E., Hotamisligil G. S., Lipid signaling and lipotoxicity in metaflammation: Indications for metabolic disease pathogenesis and treatment. J. Lipid Res. 57, 2099&#x2013;2114 (2016).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5321214</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">27330055</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kusminski C. M., Shetty S., Orci L., Unger R. H., Scherer P. E., Diabetes and apoptosis: Lipotoxicity. Ap